:0,"m_total":493750},"source_id":"unhcr-demographics-2026"}},"headlines":{"over_time":{"text":"South Sudanese refugees in Uganda rose from {n0} (2012) to a peak of {n1} (2017)","nums":[11135,1037412],"years":[2012,2017]},"where_people_are":{"text":"Uganda hosts {p0} of all South Sudanese refugees (2025), up from {p1} in 2012","pcts":[43.3,12.8],"years":[2025,2012]}},"steps":{"brief":true,"key_numbers":true,"over_time":true,"where_people_are":true,"inside_outside":true,"compare":false,"context":true,"other_angles":true,"limitations":true,"sources":true},"brief_sources":[],"footnotes":{"fn_039ff8f7":"The figure represents a rudimentary estimate of in situ stateless persons. These estimates were provided by representatives from these unrecognized communities. The estimated figures have not been verified or confirmed by the government of Uganda and UNHCR and UNHCR is planning to support government efforts to gather official statistics on stateless persons and persons of undetermined nationality in Uganda.","fn_3df86a34":"This figure presents an estimate of persons with undetermined nationality/at risk of statelessness, based on joint outreach mission conducted by the Government of Uganda and UNHCR in September/October 2021, that aimed to provide estimate numbers through self-identification of communities not recognized under the Third Schedule of the 1995 Constitution.","fn_7e86a50d":"This figure presents an estimate of persons with undetermined nationality/at risk of statelessness, based on joint outreach mission conducted by the Government of Uganda and UNHCR in September/October 2021, that aimed to provide estimate numbers through self-identification of communities not recognized under the Third Schedule of the 1995 Constitution.","fn_adf95ca4":"The figure is based on the 2024 National Housing & Population Census report which shows that there are 10,284 persons who identified themselves as members of indigenous communities, namely Bagabu, Bakingwe, Benet and Maragoli, that are not listed as nationals of Uganda in the Third Schedule to the Constitution. However, this may not represent the entirety of the stateless population in the country.","fn_c2a5d44a":"The figure is based on the 2024 National Housing & Population Census report which shows that there are 10,284 persons who identified themselves as members of indigenous communities, namely Bagabu, Bakingwe, Benet and Maragoli, that are not listed as nationals of Uganda in the Third Schedule to the Constitution. However, this may not represent the entirety of the stateless population in the country.","fn_c39ecb08":"This figure presents an estimate of persons with undetermined nationality/at risk of statelessness, based on joint outreach mission conducted by the Government of Uganda and UNHCR in September/October 2021, that aimed to provide estimate numbers through self-identification of communities not recognized under the Third Schedule of the 1995 Constitution.","fn_d4d34a8f":"IDP figure in South Sudan includes 105,000 people who are in an IDP-like situation.","fn_df527f60":"The figure is based on the 2024 National Housing & Population Census report which shows that there are 10,284 persons who identified themselves as members of indigenous communities, namely Bagabu, Bakingwe, Benet and Maragoli, that are not listed as nationals of Uganda in the Third Schedule to the Constitution. However, this may not represent the entirety of the stateless population in the country.","fn_f2456025":"An unknown number of refugees and asylum-seekers from South Sudan may be included under Sudan (in absence of separate statistics for both countries). IDP figure in South Sudan includes 105,000 people who are in an IDP-like situation."},"raw_files":{"conflict.csv":{"label":"IDMC GIDD, conflict and violence (HDX csv)","header":["iso3","country_name","year","new_displacement","new_displacement_rounded","total_displacement","total_displacement_rounded"]},"persons_of_concern.csv":{"label":"UNHCR Refu